Execute rules assigned at the site root when the site root itself is modified.

``execute_rules`` dispatches on ``aq_parent(event.object)``, and for the site
root that is the Zope application root, which cannot hold rule assignments —
while ``execute`` declines to bubble past a site root in any case. So a rule
assigned to the site root never ran for an edit to the site root, though the
control panel reported it as active and nothing errored.

This matters on a Plone 6 / Volto site, where the homepage's blocks live on the
site root and ``plone.restapi`` notifies ``ObjectModifiedEvent`` on it: the most
frequently edited page was the one page no rule ever ran for.
